Package: PORTO
Type: Package
Title: Preference and Ordinal Threshold Orientations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Thyago", family = "Nepomuceno",
    email = "nepomuceno@de.ufpe.be", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = "Department of Statistics, Federal University of Pernambuco")
Maintainer: Thyago Nepomuceno <nepomuceno@de.ufpe.be>
Description: Implements ordinal weight restrictions in data envelopment
    analysis and Benefit-of-the-Doubt composite indicators. Provides radial
    and directional multiplier formulations, weak, moderate and strict
    preference specifications, rank-based surrogate weights and pooled
    positional surrogate allocation for tied priorities. The directional
    formulations jointly account for desirable and undesirable indicators.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: lpSolve
NeedsCompilation: no
